    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "title",
      "narration": "How long does it take money to double? There is a quick mental shortcut, and people have used it for centuries. It is called the rule of seventy two. Let us see how it works.",
      "props": {
        "headline": "How fast money doubles",
        "kicker": "COMPOUND INTEREST"
      },
      "cues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "rule",
      "type": "kinetic-text",
      "narration": "Divide seventy two by the yearly interest rate. The answer is roughly how many years it takes for savings to double.",
      "props": {
        "lines": [
          "Divide",
          "seventy two",
          "by the rate"
        ]
      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "atWord": "Divide",
          "do": "emphasize",
          "text": "Divide"
        },
        {
          "atWord": "rate",
          "do": "emphasize",
          "text": "rate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nine",
      "type": "big-number",
      "narration": "At nine percent a year, seventy two divided by nine is eight. So a hundred dollars becomes two hundred in about eight years. Keep that same rate, and it doubles again eight years later.",
      "props": {
        "value": 8,
        "suffix": " yrs",
        "decimals": 0,
        "label": "to double at 9% a year",
        "factId": "f-9",
        "tone": "positive"
      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "atWord": "eight",
          "occurrence": 1,
          "do": "callout",
          "text": "Years to double"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exact",
      "type": "compare",
      "narration": "Is the shortcut accurate? At eight percent, the rule says nine years. The exact math says nine point zero zero six. That is a very tiny gap between the two answers.",
      "props": {
        "title": "Years to double at 8%",
        "suffix": " yrs",
        "decimals": 3,
        "left": {
          "label": "Rule of 72",
          "value": 9,
          "factId": "f-8rule"
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Exact math",
          "value": 9.006,
          "factId": "f-8exact"
        }
      },
      "cues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "caveat",
      "type": "kinetic-text",
      "narration": "It is an estimate, not a promise. Real returns move around from year to year, so the rule only describes a steady rate, and it leaves out taxes and fees along the way.",
      "props": {
        "lines": [
          "An estimate",
          "not a promise"
        ]
      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "atWord": "estimate",
